60,3,1,talk,Minato,,- **Minato**: I am a little confused by all these options. Which one helps the tired people the most?,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: The Field Service App is risky given the signal issues, but the Supplier Data Hub could stop the repeated certificate requests.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,"The Supplier Data Hub fits the recurring allowance, but it needs a single owner to avoid becoming another abandoned effort.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"The Hub targets a specific group, which fits the pattern of narrow tools that actually survived.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""May"",""self"":true,""raw"":""May: The Hub targets a specific group, which fits the pattern of narrow tools that actually survived.""}]}"
64,3,1,talk,Midori,,"- **Midori**: The Hub directly addresses the misrouted deliveries and the repeated copying, which are our biggest daily frustrations.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minato,,- **Minato**: But who will actually maintain the Hub? I am worried the two tired clerks will have even more work.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: If the developers are unavailable, the Hub risks becoming another undocumented mess without a clear technical steward.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,"The clerks already handle vendor queries, so the Hub would consolidate their work rather than add to it.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""George"",""self"":true,""raw"":""George: The clerks already handle vendor queries, so the Hub would consolidate their work rather than add to it.""}]}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"- **May**: Agreed. A single searchable catalog is a narrow, specific tool, exactly the kind that survived the last three rollouts.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Midori,,"- **Midori**: Agreed. It stops the weekly chaos of misrouted deliveries, which is the real pain on the floor.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minato,,"- **Minato**: I am still worried. If the developers are busy, who will build it?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: The fixed-fee vendors can build it, since their rates have held steady, unlike the per-head licences.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,"A fixed-fee build fits the recurring allowance, but we must name a single owner before signing anything.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""George"",""self"":true,""raw"":""George: A fixed-fee build fits the recurring allowance, but we must name a single owner before signing anything.""}]}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"- **May**: Agreed. A fixed-fee build avoids the per-head trap, and a narrow scope keeps it sustainable.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Midori,,"- **Midori**: Agreed. A fixed-fee build keeps costs predictable, and a single owner ensures it doesn't get abandoned.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minato,,- **Minato**: I think the Supplier Data Hub is the best choice. It helps the tired clerks and stops the mistakes.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,- **Jonathan**: Agreed. The Hub is the only option that fits our constraints and addresses the real daily problems.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,George,,"I agree. The Hub is the only candidate that fits the recurring allowance and has a clear, single owner.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,"- **May**: Agreed. The Hub is the narrow, specific tool that will actually survive its first year.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Midori,,- **Midori**: Agreed. The Hub fixes the daily friction without adding to the burden of those already stretched thin.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
